      "writtenOn": "2022-10-28T18:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s manually matching the skif::RoundOut function. When rounding out, we first inset by kRoundEpsilon so that left/top edges that are x.9999 round \"out\" to (x+1) instead of jumping all the way to x, and similarly for right/bot edges that are x.0001 round \"out\" to x instead of jumping all the way to (x+1). This has helped cut down on pixel interpolation and popping due to float transforms that should have been integers not actually staying that way.",
